[align=center]
[size=200][b]Calibration, Faceplates & Card Configuration — Complete Guide[/b][/size]
[/align]
[hr]
A recognised exact model automatically receives its registered hardware profile and recommended visible faceplate.
Calibration customises visual presentation without changing the underlying physical-device evidence.

[size=150][b]Open Calibration[/b][/size]
Use the [b]Calibrate[/b] button on a Switch Vision card. Global on-card button visibility is controlled under:
[code]Settings → Devices & services → Switch Vision → Configure[/code]

[size=150][b]What can be calibrated[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]RJ45 port centres and hitboxes
[*]port numbers
[*]Link/Speed LEDs
[*]Activity LEDs
[*]SFP/uplink positions and labels
[*]status LEDs and labels
[*]logos
[*]Status Box 1 / Status Box 2 / selected-port status box
[*]faceplate selection
[/list]

[size=150][b]Calibration Profiles[/b][/size]
Calibration Profile management is located in [b]Switch Vision Hub[/b]. The Hub can list, identify stale/duplicate, copy, import, export, protect/delete and clean stale profiles.
Core still owns calibration storage and validation. The Hub does not directly edit Home Assistant internal storage files.

[size=150][b]Faceplates[/b][/size]
Custom faceplates belong in:
[code]/config/www/switch-vision/faceplates/[/code]
Custom logos belong in:
[code]/config/www/switch-vision/logos/[/code]
A faceplate cannot be hidden. Keep custom filenames stable because each faceplate has its own saved profile namespace.

[size=150][b]Reset behaviour[/b][/size]
[b]Reset Current Switch[/b] returns the current switch to its appropriate registered/default profile.
[b]Reset All Switches[/b] should only be used when you intentionally want to remove saved calibration from every switch.
[warning]Do not use Reset as a routine troubleshooting step when custom topology should be preserved.[/warning]

[size=150][b]Safety[/b][/size]
Imported calibration is validated before replacing the active profile. Unsafe coordinates, invalid dimensions, path traversal, excessive payloads or unreasonable element counts are rejected. A rejected import leaves the current profile intact.
